+{"attempts":0,"blocked_reason":null,"blocked_since":null,"blocks":[],"capability_tags":["duckbrain","http","reliability"],"ci_result":null,"commit_hash":null,"completed_at":null,"complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-09-21T00:28:47.802316+00:00","depends_on":[],"dispatched_at":null,"exit_code":null,"fallback_model":null,"fallback_provider":null,"files_changed":[],"foreman_note":null,"guard_result":null,"id":"AUG-011","lines_added":0,"lines_removed":0,"perpetual":null,"primary_model":null,"primary_provider":null,"priority":"P2","reasoning":"DuckBrain's HTTP API runs a token-bucket limiter (src/auth/ratelimit.ts; live limit measured at 600 requests/minute per IP, X-RateLimit-Limit: 600). auger hit it in two distinct ways during this tick: (a) the transport had no retry, so a 429 propagated to the caller and cmd_init then read the ERROR body as a namespace list and crashed ('str' object has no attribute 'get') while leaving its namespace behind; (b) a test namespace leaked because the teardown DELETE itself 429'd. (a) is fixed in auger (d2dcad3: bounded retry honouring retryAfter/Retry-After, plus init failing loudly on a non-200 list). (b) is NOT fixed: teardown_namespace does not retry, so a 429 during teardown still leaks a registry row. Separately, and this one is DuckBrain's, not auger's: DELETE /api/namespaces/<n> leaves NO record of a namespace whose directory is gone — 19 stale test entries accumulated in /api/namespaces (cleared by hand this tick) because the directory removal and the registry delete are independent. Scope: (i) auger teardown retries on 429; (ii) check whether the stale-registry class is DuckBrain-wide (it affects any tool that creates namespaces) and file it against the duckbrain board if so.","review_notes":null,"status":"pending","title":"[P2] DuckBrain's 429 backpressure is unhandled by every caller (found by AUG-006's tier-1 judge)","updated_at":"2026-09-21T00:28:47.802316+00:00","worker_status":"pending","worker_summary":null,"detail":{"fing